    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_b1_plans_predictions_future_forms",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "b1-plans-predictions-01",
        "slug": "b1-plans-predictions-future-forms",
        "title": "Choosing future forms",
        "rule_summary": "Use present continuous for fixed arrangements, going to for intentions/evidence, and will for spontaneous decisions or neutral predictions.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای قرار قطعی از present continuous، برای قصد یا شواهد از going to و برای تصمیم لحظه‌ای یا پیش‌بینی خنثی از will استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "I'm seeing Sam tonight.",
            "fa": "امشب سام رو می‌بینم."
          },
          {
            "en": "I'll answer the phone.",
            "fa": "من تلفن رو جواب می‌دم."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "B1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_b1_plans_predictions_prediction_strength",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "b1-plans-predictions-02",
        "slug": "b1-plans-predictions-prediction-strength",
        "title": "Prediction adverbs",
        "rule_summary": "Use probably, definitely, perhaps, and likely to show how certain a prediction is.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با probably، definitely، perhaps و likely میزان اطمینان پیش‌بینی را نشان می‌دهیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "It'll probably take an hour.",
            "fa": "احتمالاً یک ساعت طول می‌کشه."
          },
          {
            "en": "She's definitely going to notice.",
            "fa": "قطعاً متوجه می‌شه."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "B1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_b1_plans_predictions_if_future",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "b1-plans-predictions-03",
        "slug": "b1-plans-predictions-if-future",
        "title": "Future with first conditional",
        "rule_summary": "Use if + present simple for a possible condition and will/might/can for the result.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای شرط ممکن از if + present simple و برای نتیجه از will/might/can استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "If traffic is bad, we'll take the train.",
            "fa": "اگر ترافیک بد باشه، قطار می‌گیریم."
          },
          {
            "en": "If we finish early, we might go out.",
            "fa": "اگر زود تموم کنیم، شاید بریم بیرون."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "B1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
